   "text": "```python\n\"\"\"\nLRU Cache with Time-To-Live (TTL) Expiry\n\nThis module implements a thread-safe Least Recently Used (LRU) cache that\nautomatically expires entries after a configurable Time-To-Live (TTL).\n\nKey Features:\n- LRU eviction policy: when the cache reaches its maximum capacity,\n  the least recently accessed item is evicted.\n- TTL support: each entry has an absolute expiry time. Entries that have\n  expired are removed lazily on access.\n- Thread safety: the cache is protected by a reentrant lock (RLock) so that\n  multiple threads can safely read/write without corrupting state.\n- Pytest test suite: includes comprehensive tests for basic operations,\n  TTL expiry, LRU eviction, thread safety, and edge cases.\n\nThe implementation is divided into two main parts:\n1. lru_ttl_cache: The core cache logic.\n2. tests: A pytest test suite that validates the cache behavior.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport threading\nimport time\nfrom collections import OrderedDict\nfrom typing import Any, Callable, Generic, TypeVar, Optional\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Type Aliases\n# -",
